::PC_U05_L05_Q01::
Question ID: PC_U05_L05_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.PC.PA.4
Question:
Which statement is correct about parabolas?
{
~A. Every parabola opens upward.#This choice misses the key feature structure of this conic. Identify the conic definition and equation form before choosing an answer.
=B. The vertex is a key feature used to graph and interpret the parabola.#Correct. The vertex helps locate the parabola and interpret its turning point.
~C. The focus and directrix are never related to a parabola.#This choice misses the key feature structure of this conic. Identify the conic definition and equation form before choosing an answer.
~D. A parabola has a constant radius from a center.#This choice misses the key feature structure of this conic. Identify the conic definition and equation form before choosing an answer.
}
